**The answer is three-fold:**

1. **Cost barrier:** Every existing quality testing solution requires hardware costing ₹2 Lakh to ₹20 Lakh. There are 80 million dairy households in India. The math doesn't work.

2. **Regulatory gap:** BIS IS 19562:2026 was released in **May 2026**. No existing product was designed around this standard because it didn't exist until 4 months ago. We are the **first mover** on regulatory compliance tooling.

3. **Ecosystem gap:** Existing global solutions (FOSS, Alltech, trinamiX) don't integrate with India's government digital livestock infrastructure (INAPH, Bharat Pashudhan, e-GOPALA, AMCS). Our system can.

